936;10262;%4%1 Softstart fault power supply unit (F:2816);1. Inadmissible voltage variations in the supply mains. Mains voltage has dropped inadmissibly during the soft start process%CrLf%2. Short-circuit in the DC intermediate circuit%CrLf%3. Load at the DC intermediate circuit%CrLf%4. Insulation fault in the DC intermediate circuit%CrLf%5. Final value of the intermediate circuit voltage is not reached within a maximum time;1. Switch drive control device to idle (5 seconds) and then restart controller. Check mains voltage%CrLf%2. Check intermediate circuit wiring, if there is any short-circuit, eliminate it%CrLf%3. Check intermediate circuit wiring, if there is any faulty connection of an external brake resistor, make correct connection%CrLf%4. Check intermediate circuit wiring, if wiring is ok, there may be an insulation fault inside the device or at further devices connected to the intermediate circuit. To localize the defective device, remove the connected devices step by step from the drive package (remove wiring)%CrLf%5. Check whether there is any defect at the consumer that is externally connected to the intermediate circuit.
