2236;167;%1: Configured parameter %2 not possible in actual values (AT).;A configured cyclic actual-value can't be transmitted cyclic because it is not contained in list of cyclic actual-values (S-0-0187);Check configuration
2236;168;%1: Invalid SERCOS parameter switching to phase %2: %3.;One or more parameters of the drive are not valid. That was detected on sercos phase switch preparation.;Parameter values must be changed
2236;169;%1: Drive not ready for power on (SERCOS drive state 0x%2).;In drivecom state 'ready to switch on' drive signalled in sercos stateword S-0-0135 the state 'drive not ready for power on' (bits 14 and 15 are 0).;Check drive and its power supply.
2236;170;%1: Drive not ready or power not applied (SERCOS drive state 0x%2).;In drivecom state 'switched on' drive signalled in sercos stateword S-0-0135 a cleared bit 15.;Check drive and its power supply.
2236;171;%1: Drive not possible to switch on, power not applied (SERCOS drive state 0x%2).;Drivecom state transition 3 'Switch on' is not possible, because drive signals in stateword S-0-0135 via bit 15, that power is not applied.;Check drive and its power supply.
2236;172;%1: '%2' set value exceeds range (value: %3, factor: %4).;A set-value transformation from user units (endpoint value) to drive units using the configured transformation factor resulted a range overflow.;Check configuration of transformation factors and/or set-value calculation.
2236;173;%1: Auxiliary set value '%2' exceeds range (value: %3, factor: %4).;A addtional set-value transformation from user units (endpoint value) to drive units using the  transformation factor read from drive (parameter attribute) resulted a range overflow.;Check addional set-values.
2236;174;%1: Invalid SERCOS cycle time configured (%2 us).;Check of cycle time done by sercos hardware is not successful (number of devices, length of process data).;Check configuration concerning cycle time, number of devices and length of process data.
2236;175;%1: SERCOS ring not closed.;For SERCOS 2: Sercos ring is not closed. Most common reason is, that at least one configured device was not detected. For SERCOS III: No devices detected.;Check of sercos wiring and devices.
2236;176;%1: State Param-Set-Write:  nr=%2, wr=%3, err=%4.;The parameter set for the given device has been loaded from a file to the device.;Nothing to do for the user.
2236;177;%1: State Param-Set-Read:  nr=%2, rd=%3, err=%4.;The parameter set for the drive has been stored to a file.;Nothing to do.
2236;178;%1: ignoreMessage not supported.;The ignoreMessage config parameter is not supported for the connected device.;Remove configuration parameter.
2236;179;%1: Drive state can't be changed while Statusreport is active;The application tried to switch the drive to "Drive halt" or "Drive enabled" while a statusreport was active.;Wait until the statusreport has finished
2236;180;%1: Duplicate SERCOS-address detected on bus.;Several SERCOS-devices on the bus are using the same SERCOS-address.;Check SERCOS device addresses
2236;181;%1: Invalid SERCOS-address detected on bus.;A device with an invalid SERCOS-address was detected on the bus.;Check SERCOS device addresses.
2236;182;%1: Device version not supported.;At least one device uses an unsupported SERCOS-version.;Unplug the device that uses an unsupported SERCOS-version.
2236;183;%1: Maximum MDT-telegram count exceeded.;The maximum count of 4 MDT-telegrams does not suffice to transfer all cyclic data in MDT.;Check configuration. Configure less cyclic output data.
2236;184;%1: Maximum AT-telegram count exceeded.;The maximum count of 4 AT-telegrams does not suffice to transfer all cyclic data in AT.;Check configuration. Configure less cyclic input data.
2236;185;%1: Too much data configured for bus cycletime (%2 s).;The configured bus cycletime does not suffice to transfer all data.;Check configuration. Configure less cyclic data or a greater cycle time.
2236;186;%1: Wrong connection count for SCP_FixCFG (%2 expected).;Configuration error. The connection count for a device that uses SCP_FixCFG is invalid.;Correct connection count in configuration.
2236;187;%1: Too many connections configured (%2 allowed).;Configuration error. Too many connections are configured for a device.;Configure less connections.
2236;188;%1: Duplicate connection number %2.;Configuration error. The connection number is used more than once.;Configure unique connection number.
2236;189;%1: Inconsistent data length of connection %2.;Configuration error. The data length of a connection does not match the data length calculated by the device.;correct data length.
2236;190;%1: Inconsistent cycle time of connection %2.;Configuration error. A connection was configured with different cycle times.;Correct configured cycle time.
2236;191;%1: Length of connection %2 is larger than maximum length.;Configuration error. The length of a connection is larger than its maximum allowed length.;Reduce connection length.
2236;192;%1: Consumed connection %2 not produced.;Configuration error. A consumer connection was configured without an associated producer connection.;Configure associated producer connection.
2236;193;%1: No %2 connections projected in engineering data file.;Configuration error. No connections projected for device.;Project connections.
2236;194;%1: Failed to add %2 connection (connection number = %3).;Configuration error. Failed to add a producer or consumer connection.;Check connection parameters
2236;195;%1: Projected data length %2 of connection %3 does not match expected value %4.;Configuration error. The projected data length of a connection does not match the length calculated from the attributes of the parameters.;correct projected connection length
2236;196;%1: Projected size %2 of variable for IDN %3 does not match expected value %4.;Configuration error. The projected size of a variable does not match the size calculated from the attribute of the parameter.;correct length
2236;197;%1: Projected offset %2 of variable for IDN %3 does not match expected value %4.;Configuration error. The projected offset of a variable does not match the offset calculated from the attribute of the parameter.;correct offset
2236;198;%1: Variable %2 in process mapping not used because of configuration entry %3.;Inconsistency between configuration and projection. A projected variable is not used because of a configuration entry.;If the data is supposed to be available the the configuration entry should be corrected. If the data shall not be available the projected variable should be deleted from the process image.
2236;199;%1: Value %2 for entry %3 in engineering data file is not supported.;Configuration error. A value projected in the engineering data file is not supported.;correct the unsupported value in the engineering data file
2236;200;%1: Inconsistence detected in engineering data file.;Configuration error. Inconsistency exists in engineering data file.;Resolve inconsistence in engineering data file.
2236;201;%1: Engineering data file '%2' not found.;The engineering data file was not found;Adapt path to engineering data file or put engineering data file to specified path
2236;202;%1: Malformed engineering data file (XML syntax error).;Configuration error. The engineering data file is no XML file or contains an XML syntax error.;Chech whether the XML syntax is correct in the engineering data file
2236;203;%1: Value '%2' for XML node '%3' in engineering data file is not valid.;Configuration error. The engineering data file contains an in valid value.;Correct the specified invalid value.
2236;204;%1: Mandatory XML node '%2' missing in engineering data file.;Configuration error. Mandatory XML node missing in engineering data file.;Insert the missing node.
2236;205;%1: Mandatory XML node '%2' in engineering data file is empty.;Configuration error. No value specified for mandatory XML node.;Specify value for node
2236;206;%1: No variable found for IDN %2 in engineering data file.;Configuration error. No variable could be found for an IDN in the engineering data file.;Resolve error in engineering data file
2236;207;%1: Device not found in engineering data file (address=%2).;Configuration error. The device could not be found in the engineering data file.;Resolve error in engineering data file or in configuration file.
2236;208;%1: Value for configuration entry '%2' conflicts with one or more values in the engineering data file.;Inconsistency between configuration and projection. Value for a configuration entry conflicts with one or more a value in the engineering data file.;Resolve error in engineering data file or in configuration file.
2236;209;%1: Multiple consumers for one connection are not supported (connection number = %2).;Configuration error. A connection in the engineering data file has more than one consumer.;Project only one consumer per connection
2236;210;%1: Parameter action error (IDN = '%2', action = '%3', errCode = %4, errState = %5, timeOut = %6).;Error on parameter action;Activate trace of [Serc100M], [...SERCOS3:X] and [...S3DEVICE:Y] to get more detailled information about the error cause
2236;211;%1: Value '%2' for parameter '%3' does not match expected value '%4'.;A parameter value compared with the parameter action RDCMP does not match the expected value;Check configuration or device parametrization.
2236;212;%1: Value for parameter %2 does not match expected value.;The value of a parameter does not match the projected / expected value;Check configuration or device parametrization.
2236;213;%1: Slave valid bit already set when changing to phase %2.;Error in device. Behaviour not according to SERCOS specification. A device has set the 'slave valid'-bit.;Replace device causing this error
2236;214;%1: Slave valid bit not set when changing to phase %2;Error in device. Behaviour not according to SERCOS specification. A device has not set the 'slave valid'-bit.;Replace device causing this error
2236;215;%1: Error in parameter access by driver in phase %2;A parameter transfer initiated by the low level driver when changing a phase failed.;Check connection to device, check availability of needed parameters on device
2236;216;%1: Outputs are not activated.;Error in device. The device has not set the 'outputs ready-to-operate' bit in the status word (S-0-1500.0.2).;Contact device manufacturer
2236;217;%1: Input values are not valid.;Error in device. The device has not set the 'inputs valid' bit in the status word (S-0-1500.0.2).; The input values are not valid"
2236;218;%1: I/O error: text = %2, SERCOS standard = %3, class = %4, diagnostic number = %5;The device has set the 'I/O error' bit in the status word (S-0-1500.0.2);"see diagnostic number (S-0-0390), text (if available) and manufacturer's data
2236;219;%1: I/O error cleared;I/O error has been reset;no interaction necessary
2236;220;%1: I/O warning: text = %2, SERCOS standard = %3, class = %4, diagnostic number = %5;The device has set the 'I/O warning' bit in the status word (S-0-1500.0.2).;see diagnostic number (S-0-0390), text (if available) and manufacturer's data
2236;221;%1: I/O warning gone;The reason for the previous warning has gone;no interaction necessary
2236;222;%1: I/O info: text = %2, SERCOS standard = %3, class = %4, diagnostic number = %5;The device has set the 'I/O info' bit in the status word (S-0-1500.0.2).;see diagnostic number (S-0-0390), text (if available) and manufacturer's data
2236;223;%1: Bustopology changed from '%2' to '%3';Bus topology changed due to connected or disconnected network cable.;If no change of the bus topology was desired, the network cables in use should be checked.
2236;224;%1: Ring break between %2 and %3;Ring break due to disconnected network cable, for example.;If no change of the bus topology was desired, the network cables in use should be checked.
2236;225;%1: Inconsistent data length of connection %2 (expected %3, configured %4).;Configuration error. The data length of a connection does not match the data length calculated by the device.;Correct the data length of the connection(actualDataLength) in the SCI.
2236;226;%1: Duplicate SERCOS-address (%2) detected on bus.;Several SERCOS-devices on the bus are using the same SERCOS-address.;Check SERCOS device addresses.
2236;227;%1: Invalid SERCOS-address (%2) detected on bus.;A device with an invalid SERCOS-address has been detected on the bus.;Check SERCOS device addresses.
2236;228;%1: Error setting addresses: could not get device count;Systeminternal error on getting device count from Interface. Bus may be in wrong phase.;Contact distributor.
2236;229;%1: Error setting addresses: could not get device info;Systeminternal error on getting device info from Interface. Bus may be in wrong phase.;Contact distributor.
2236;230;%1: Can not set addresses due to configuration error of device %2;Automatic address setting is only possible when the configuration of all devices is correct.;Resolve configuration error.
2236;231;%1: XML node '%2' necessary for setting addresses missing in engineering data file;Configuration error. A XML node needed for autmoatic address setting is missing in the engineering data file. For automatic address setting the nodes 'vendorCode' and 'vendorDeviceID' have to be projected for each device.;Add missing XML node to projection.
2236;232;%1: Error setting addresses: Actual device count (%2) different from configuration (%3);The number of connected devices is different from the number of configured devices. The number of configured devices does not include simulated devices.;Adjust configuration or connected devices.
2236;233;%1: Error setting addresses: Electronic type label (%2, %3) not projected;An electronic type label found on bus does not match any projected electronic type label (vendorCode and vendorDeviceID).;Project correct electronic type label for all connected devices.
2236;234;%1: Device order mismatch;Electronic type label and addresses of devices on bus match the configuration, but the order of the devices does not match.;Adjust projection or topology such that the order of the devices matches.
2236;235;%1: Size %2 of IDN %3 not supported in cyclic data;Configuration error. The actual length of a parameter is not supported in cyclic data, because it does not match the endpoint size.;Do not configure cyclic IDN with unsupported length.
2236;236;%1: Error in parameter access by driver in phase %2 for IDN %3;A parameter transfer in consequence of system bootup when changing a phase failed.;Check connection to device, check availability or value of specified parameter on device
2236;237;%1: Affected typelabel: vendorCode %2 and vendorDeviceID %3 (typelabel of %4);Additional Information about first affected device of error with automatic address setting or topology check.;Same solution as previous displayed error.
2236;238;%1: Calculated ring delay too small;The calculated ring delay is smaller than the measured one. The problem is caused by too many unconfigured SERCOS devices or other devices on the bus.;Unplug unconfigured slaves.
2236;239;%1: Device order and addresses mismatch;The device order and the addresses on the bus do not match the projection.;Adjust projection or topology such that the order of the devices matches.
2236;240;%1: Changing SERCOS address %2 to %3;Due to automatic address setting or topology check the displayed address is changed on the device;no interaction necessary
2236;241;%1: Too many IDNs (%2) configured for connection %3. (max = %4);Too many IDNs are configured in a connection.;Check projection, configure less modules.
2236;242;%1: Produced connection %2 not consumed.;Configuration error. A producer connection was configured without an associated consumer connection.;Configure associated consumer connection.
2236;243;%1: Slave reported error in parameter access in phase %2 for IDN %3;The Slave reported a failure of a parameter transfer in consequence of system bootup when changing a phase.;Check availability or value of specified parameter on device
2237;1;%1: unit '%2' already configured;multiple equipment-configuration;Check the configuration-files
2237;2;%1: auto pci configuration not possible, there is more than one device of that type;There are more pci devices of that type in system. Auto configuration for pci devices is only possible if there is only one device of a type in system. It must be pointed out, that internal pci device (e.g. network controller) are also included at checking auto configuration.;Pci configuration (slot and if applicable bus) must be used in config file.
2237;3;%1: bad dll locked quality (events %2, actual state %3);The dll device state is not locked.;Check dll configuration (cycle time) and system capacity.
2237;4;%1: dll locked;The dll device state is locked.; 
2238;1;%1: Asi slave state: %2;Error for Asi-Slave reported; 
2238;2;%1: Asi slave state ok;No error for Asi-Slave reported; 
