4000;407;Kinematic %1: Drive '%2' in wrong position mode (%3, expected: %4);The position mode of the drive does not match the the joint type of the kinematic joint. For modulo joints the drive has to be actuated in position mode 'Raw-Mode'.;Check the configuration.
4000;408;Kinematic %1 (Joint %2): Setting position not possible. Kinematic is started.;The joint's position cannot be set since the kinematic is in state 'started'.;The joint's position must be set before calling McuRestart() or McuStartInterpolator().
4000;409;Kinematic %1 (Joint %2): Setting position not possible. Drive in error state.;The position cannot be set when the actual position of the drive is not available. Therefore the drive must not be in an error state or booting.;The error state of the drive must be resetted or the boot up sequence of the drive has to be finished first.
4000;410;Kinematic %1 (Joint %2): Setting position not possible. Drive is not referenced.;The position cannot be set when the actual position of the drive is not available. The drive signals 'reference lost' by its status bit.;Before setting the position of a joint the drive must be referenced or the status bit 'reference lost' has to be cleared.
4000;411;Kinematic %1 (Joint %2): Mastering not possible. Invalid reference pulse interval (%3).;"The drive cannot be mastered as the distance between two reference pulses is invalid. The distance between two reference pulses must be: a whole number; greater than 0 and smaller than 24-Bits"
4000;412;Kinematic %1 (Joint %2): Mastering not possible. Invalid gear ratio.;The drive cannot be mastered as the gear ratio is not a whole number.;not available
4000;413;Kinematic %1 (joint %2): Referencing using reference pulse: No master value available.;The position of the drive cannot be set by using reference pulse as there is no master value available.;The drive must be mastered first.
4000;414;Kinematic %1 (joint %2): Distance to reference pulse too big.;The position of the drive cannot be set by using reference pulse because the distance to the master position ist too big. The distance must not exceed +90‹/-90‹ of the drive.;The position where the drive has been mastered must be approached more closely.
4000;415;Kinematic %1 (joint %2): Mastering/referencing not supported. Joint depends on modulo drive (joint %3).;The joint cannot be mastered or referenced as the position of the joint depends on a modulo drive by a gear. This is not supported.;not available
4000;416;Kinematic %1 (joint %2): Setting position not possible. Master axis not referenced (joint %3).;The joint's position cannot be set, because the joint depends on another joint (master joint) by a gear, which is not referenced yet.;The master joint must be referenced first.
4000;417;Kinematic %1 (Joint %2): Mastering not possible. Drive is a Modulo Drive.;Mastering a Modulo Drive is not possible because they implement the modulo funcionality theirselves;The joint can only be referenced wihout using an index pulse.
4000;420;Kinematic %1 (joint %2): Drive has lost reference.;A drive of the kinematic lost its reference.;The drive and the joint must be referenced again.
