6353;2;%1: At least one Ethernet frame was lost in the EtherCAT segment.;Error in the EtherCAT segment or hot connect of an EtherCAT slave.;Check correct operation of slaves and cabling in the EtherCAT segment. If a hot connect was done, then ignore this message.
6353;3;%1: Invalid EtherCAT frame was received.;Error in the EtherCAT segment.;Check correct operation of slaves and cabling of the EtherCAT segment.
6353;4;%1: '%2' is not a correct XML file.;The XML file is malformed.;Correct XML file.
6353;5;%1: '%2': Node '%3' has invalid value '%4' (section = '%5' / '%6').;The node in the XML file has an invalid value.;Correct value of node.
6353;6;%1: Memory area %2.%3 - %4.%5 is not received.;No cyclic command reads this memory area.;Add cyclic command or correct memory area.
6353;7;%1: Memory area %2.%3 - %4.%5 is not sent.;No cyclic command writes this memory area.;Add cyclic command or correct memory area.
6353;8;%1: Number of slaves in the EtherCAT segment (%2) is invalid.;The configuration does not support this number of slaves.;Adapt either the configuration or the number of slaves in the EtherCAT segment.
6353;9;%1: Slave at position %2 does not match configured Slave (%3: configured = %4, actually = %5).;The configured slave is different from the actual slave in the EtherCAT segment.;Correct the configuration of the slave or add the right slave to the EtherCAT segment.
6353;10;%1: Node address %2 not found in projection.;A node address, which does not match any node address in the projection, was configured.;Correct configuration or projection.
6353;11;%1: Update of cyclic command %2 failed.;Update of process data of cyclic command failed, because of an internal error.;Fatal error. Please contact manufacturer.
6353;12;%1: Cyclic command %2 recovered from update error.;Update of process data of cyclic command was successful again after it failed.;No action is necessary.
6353;13;%1: Working counter of cyclic command %2 is invalid (expected = %3, received = %4).;At least one slave has not processed the cyclic command as expected.;If the working counter continues to return with a wrong value, then at least one defect slave must be replaced in the EtherCAT segment. Otherwise an adequate message is dropped.
6353;14;%1: Working counter of cyclic command %2 is valid again.;All slaves processed the cyclic command as expected again.;No action is necessary.
6353;15;%1: Transmission of Ethernet frames failed.;An Ethernet Frame was not sent, because the CPU power is not sufficient for the requested bus load.;Reduce the bus load or the number of slaves in the EtherCAT segment, if the EtherCAT segment is very big. Use a more powerful CPU, if the EtherCAT segment is small.
6353;16;%1: '%2': Node '%3' is missing (section = '%4' / '%5').;A mandatory node is missing in XML file.;Add node.
6353;17;%1: Distributed Clocks are not supported.;Slave does not support Distributed Clock, even though it is required. Distributed Clock support of a slave is required if the EtherCAT segment branches at this slave or if this slave is configured for Distributed Clocks operation.;Use slave with Distributed Clocks support or change configuration and topology respectively in a way, that no Distributed Clocks support is required anymore.
6353;18;%1: Shift Time %2ns is beyond its limits (%3ns - %4ns).;The Shift Time is not within the possible range.;Choose Shift Time within limits.
6353;19;%1: Number of slaves in the EtherCAT segment (%2) is valid.;The number of slaves in the EtherCAT segment was invalid and has become valid again.;The EtherCAT segment must have a valid number of slaves.
6353;20;%1: Slaves match the configuration.;Slaves did not match the configuration and now match the configuration.;The EtherCAT segment must consist only of configured slaves.
6353;21;%1: Init command '%2' failed during state transition '%3' (AL Status Code = %4).;An init command failed during a state transition of the EtherCAT slave.;Check the failed init command.
6353;22;%1: Transition to state '%2' (AL Status Code = %3).;The EtherCAT slave has unexpectedly changed its state.;Identify reason for the state transition of the slave.
6353;23;%1: Receive data configuration invalid (address-start=%2, end=%3, max. possible length=%4).;Receive data configuration is invalid. The range configured for the station with start-address and length is too big (restriction of controller-firmware).;Adaption of receive data configuration.
6353;24;%1: Transmit data configuration invalid (address-start=%2, end=%3, max. possible length=%4).;Transmit data configuration is invalid. The range configured for the station with start-address and length is too big (restriction of controller-firmware).;Adaption of transmit data configuration.
6353;25;%1: '%2': The number of nodes '%3' is invalid (act = %4, min = %5, max = %6, section = '%7' / '%8').;The number of nodes is invalid.;Correct the number of nodes.
6353;26;%1: The cyclic commands have too many different cycle times (max = %2).;The cyclic commands are sent with too many different cycle times.;Reduce the number of different cycle times of the cyclic commands.
6353;27;%1: Too many cycles in one period (act = %2, max = %3).;"The cyclic commands are sent with too many different or too different cycle times. Too different are;The operation of the EtherCAT segment is not possible.
6353;28;%1: Node address %2 is already used.;The node address is used by at least two configured slaves.;Correct configuration.
6353;29;%1: Mailbox state is not included in any cyclic command.;The address of the mailbox state is not read by any cyclic command.;Add cyclic command, which reads the mailbox state.
6353;30;%1: Maximum number of slaves in EtherCAT segment is too high (act = %2, max = %3).;The number of configured slaves is higher than the maximum number of slaves which can be managed.;Reduce the number of configured slaves.
6353;31;%1: %2: Init command '%3' is missing (section = '%4' / '%5').;A required init command does not exist.;Add the required init command or change the configuration.
6353;32;%1: The duration of the cyclic commands is too long (act = %2, max = %3).;The transmission of the cyclic commandos takes too long.;Reduce the number or the length of the cyclic commands.
6353;33;%1: Ethernet frames were received successful again.;After the loss of at least one Ethernet frame multiple Ethernet frames were received successful.;No action is necessary.
6353;34;%1: The topology scan of the EtherCAT segment failed.;Due to missing or inconsistent information, calculation of the EtherCAT topology is not possible.;Check the correctness of the EtherCAT segment.
6353;35;%1: %2: Node '%3' is inconsistent (section = '%4' / '%5').;Slaves with the same type (Vendor ID, Product Code) must define a consistent value or content for this node. The value or content of this node is not consistent for all slaves with the same type.;Make value or content of this node consistent for all slaves with the same type.
6353;36;%1: Station alias '%2' is used by the slaves at position '%3' and '%4'.;At least two slaves have the same Station Alias.;Configure a unique station alias for this slaves.
6353;37;%1: The topology scan of the EtherCAT segment was successful.;The topology of the EtherCAT segment was invalid and is now valid again.;The topology of the EtherCAT segment must be always valid.
6353;38;%1: Mandatory slave not found (vendor ID = %2, product code = %3).;A mandatory slave does not exist in the EtherCAT segment.;Add mandatory slave to the EtherCAT segment or adapt configuration.
6353;39;%1: Unexpected slave found at position %2 (vendor ID = %3, product code = %4).;A slave exists in the EtherCAT segment, which is not configured.;Remove slave from the EtherCAT segment or adapt configuration.
6353;40;%1: The size of the hot connect group at position %2 with station alias %3 is invalid (act = %4, exp = %5).;The size of the hot connect group is different to the configured size.;Change size of hot connect group or adapt configuration
6353;41;%1: Hot connect.;Hot connect device was added to the EtherCAT segment.;None.
6353;42;%1: Hot disconnect.;Hot connect device was removed from the EtherCAT segment.;None.
6353;43;%1: %2: Auto increment address not allowed (section = '%3' / '%4').;Auto increment addressing is used during a state transition, which does not allow this addressing.;Do not use auto increment addressing.
6353;44;%1: %2: SII access not allowed (section = '%3' / '%4').;SII is accessed during a state transition, which does not allow this access.;Do not access SII.
6353;45;%1: '%2': Mailbox '%3' is too small (act = %4, min = %5, section = '%6' / '%7').;The mailbox is too small in general or it is too small for at least one of the allowed protocols.;Extend the size of the mailbox or allow less protocols.
6353;46;%1: Cycle Time 1 %2ns is beyond its limits (%3ns - %4ns).;The Cycle Time 1 is not within the possible range, because the cycle time of the EtherCAT slave is too short.;Increase cycle time of EtherCAT slave.
6353;47;%1: '%2': Mailbox '%3' has invalid size (act = %4, min = %5, max = %6, section = '%7' / '%8').;If the mailbox is too small, it is too small in general or it is too small for at least one of the allowed protocols. If the mailbox is too big, it is too big in general.;Adapt the size of the mailbox or allow less protocols.
6353;48;%1: The synchronisation of the EtherCAT segment failed.;Due to the incorrect behaviour of at least one EtherCAT slave, the synchronisation of the EtherCAT segment is not possible.;Check the correctness of the EtherCAT segment.
6353;49;%1: The synchronisation of the EtherCAT segment was successful.;The synchronisation of the EtherCAT segment was successful after it had failed before.;The synchronisation of the EtherCAT segment must be always possible.
6353;50;%1: EtherCAT segment not connected.;No EtherCAT segment is connected. The network interface has no link.;Connect EtherCAT segment.
6353;51;%1: EtherCAT segment connected.;EtherCAT segment was connected.;The EtherCAT segment must be always connected.
6353;52;%1: Ethernet frame was received too late.;An Ethernet Frame was received too late, because either the EtherCAT segment is too big for the configured cycle time or the CPU power is not sufficient for the configured cycle time.;Reduce the cycle time or the number of slaves in the EtherCAT segment, if the EtherCAT segment is very big. Use a more powerful CPU, if the EtherCAT segment is small.
6353;53;%1: Slave at position %2 is faulty (reason = %3).;Slave reports an error or violates the EtherCAT specification.;Faulty Slave must be replaced.
6353;54;%1: Invalid ECAT frame configuration (in = %2, out = %3, SYNC1 = %4);Invalid ECAT frame configuration;Correct configuration or projection.
6353;55;%1: Timing violation occurred (%2).;A timing violation occurred.;"According to the error cause the folllowing configuration entries must be increased: 'DMA': dmaTime
6353;56;%1: Timing violation cleared.;Timing is correct again.;no actions necessary
6353;57;%1: Invalid process data object order.;Invalid order of process data objects in ENI;Correct projection.
6353;58;%1: DC System time difference violation (expected max (+/-)%2 ns, actual = %3 ns).;DC System time difference (BRD on register 0x92C) is not within expected range.;Contact slave vendor.
6353;59;%1: DC System time difference violation cleared.;DC system time difference is within expected range.;No action required.
6353;60;%1: '%2': CycleTime too small (act = %3 ns, min = %4 ns, section = '%5'/'%6').;The cycle time configured in the ENI file is too small.;Use a higher cycle time.
6353;61;%1: Too many network packets with cyclic commands (max = %2);The different cycle times of master and slaves lead to too many network packets in the schedule.;The cycle times of master and slaves must be harmonized to reduce the number of network packets. E.g. reduce the biggest cycle times, and/or increase the smallest cycle times.
6353;62;%1: InputPreparationTime %2ns is beyond its limits (%3ns - %4ns).;The InputPreparationTime is not within the possible range.;Increase the cycle time of the EtherCAT slave.
6353;63;%1: Memory area %2.%3 - %4.%5 is not received completely.;No cyclic command reads this memory area completely.;Add cyclic command or correct memory area.
6353;64;%1: Memory area %2.%3 - %4.%5 is not sent completely.;No cyclic command writes this memory area completely.;Add cyclic command or correct memory area.
6353;65;%1: Slave at position %2 does not match configured slave '%3' (%4: configured = %5, actually = %6).;The configured slave is different from the actual slave in the EtherCAT segment.;Correct the configuration of the slave or add the right slave to the EtherCAT segment.
6353;66;%1: Mandatory slave '%2' not found (vendor ID = %3, product code = %4).;A mandatory slave does not exist in the EtherCAT segment.;Add mandatory slave to the EtherCAT segment or adapt configuration.
6353;67;%1: Slave is not of type '%2';The configured EtherCAT slave type does not match with the type from the engineering data file (ENI);Adapt the configuration file (cfg) or the the engineering data file (ENI).
6353;68;%1: FMMUs %2 and %3 overlap;The logical address ranges of the two FMMUs overlap. If bit addresses are used, there must be at least 3 fill bytes in between.;Adapt the engineering data file (ENI).
6353;69;%1: Slave at position %2 is faulty (reason = %3, could be slave '%4').;Slave reports an error or violates the EtherCAT specification.;Faulty Slave must be replaced.
6353;70;%1: Invalid ip address '%2';The configured ip address could not be set.;Correct configuration (cfg).
6632;1;Another application is already connected to the board number %1.;The board that should be selected is used by another application.;Exit the other application that is connected to the board and try to connect again.
