6795;2;%1: Write SERCOS parameter %2 failed (%3, %4);Writing a sercos parameter during initialization (sercos phase bootup) returned an error.;Cause can be narrowed by error code (3rd parameter). A specific SERCOS error code is shown in the trace if the traceWord is activated.
6795;3;%1: Read element %2 of SERCOS parameter %3 failed (%4);Reading a sercos parameter during initialization (sercos phase bootup) or error acknowledgment returned an error.;Cause can be narrowed by error code (3rd parameter). A specific SERCOS error code is shown in the trace if the traceWord is activated.
6795;53;%1: Drive not ready to operate (SERCOS drive state 0x%2);An error occurred in the drive control system. In drivecom state 'operation enabled' drive signalled in sercos stateword S-0-0135 via bits 14 and 15, that sercos state 'in operation, with torque' is not active.;Eliminate error reason in drive - it could be caused by the controller (e.g. invalid set values) or by the drive environment (e.g. power supply).
6795;55;%1: SERCOS class1 error occurred: 0x%2 - %3;An error occurred in the drive control system. Drive signalled a class1-error in state word S-0-0135.;Eliminate error reason in drive - it could be caused by the controller (e.g. invalid set values) or by the drive environment (e.g. power supply). The cause can be narrowed by the diagnosis text (2nd parameter).
6795;60;%1: Timeout on DRIVECOM state transition %2;Timeout occured on performing a drivecom state change during not-fulfilled conditions (e.g. halt of drives).;Check drive parameters. Leaving drivecom state 'operation enabled' drive must not move.
6795;70;%1: Change SERCOS ring phase inhibited, drive controller(s) in wrong state;Sercos phase switch is only possible, if all drives are in drivecom state 'fault' or 'switch on disabled'.;Check application.
6795;151;%1: SERCOS class2 warning occurred: 0x%2 - %3;A warning occurred in the drive control system. Drive signalled a class2-warning in state word S-0-0135.;Eliminate warning reason on drive. The cause can be narrowed by the diagnosis text (2nd parameter).
6795;163;%1: Execute SERCOS command %2 failed (%3, %4);Execution of a command during initialization (sercos phase bootup) or error acknowledgment returned an error.;Cause can be narrowed by error code (3rd parameter). A specific SERCOS error code is shown in the trace if the traceWord is activated.
6795;168;%1: Invalid SERCOS parameter switching to phase %2: %3;One or more parameters of the device are not valid. That was detected on sercos phase switch preparation.;Parameter values must be changed
6795;169;%1: Drive not ready for power on (SERCOS drive state 0x%2);An error occurred in the drive control system. In drivecom state 'ready to switch on' drive signalled in sercos stateword S-0-0135 the state 'drive not ready for power on' (bits 14 and 15 are 0).;Check drive wiring and its power supply.
6795;170;%1: Drive not ready or power not applied (SERCOS drive state 0x%2);An error occurred in the drive control system. In drivecom state 'switched on' drive signalled in sercos stateword S-0-0135 a cleared bit 15.;Check drive wiring and its power supply.
6795;171;%1: Drive not possible to switch on, power not applied (SERCOS drive state 0x%2);An error occurred in the drive control system. Drivecom state transition 3 'Switch on' is not possible, because drive signals in stateword S-0-0135 via bit 15, that power is not applied.;Check drive wiring and its power supply.
6795;176;%1: State Param-Set-Write:  nr=%2, wr=%3, err=%4;The parameter set for the given drive has been loaded from a file to the drive.;Nothing to do for the user.
6795;177;%1: State Param-Set-Read:  nr=%2, rd=%3, err=%4;The parameter set for the device has been stored to a file.;Nothing to do.
6795;178;%1: ignoreMessage not supported;The ignoreMessage config parameter is not supported for the connected drive. The Parameter for the diagnosis text (S-0-0095) could not be read.;Remove configuration parameter.
6795;179;%1: Drive state can't be changed while Statusreport is active;The application tried to switch the drive to "Drive halt" or "Drive enabled" while a statusreport was active.;Wait until the statusreport has finished
6795;180;%1: Invalid SERCOS parameter after writing parameter set: %2;One or more parameter values of the device are not valid. That was detected after writing a parameter set.;Parameter values must be changed
6795;181;%1: Execute SERCOS user command %2 failed (%3);Execution of a Sercos-command triggered by application failed. For details see command error code.;Parameter values must be changed. The cause can be narrowed by the parameter command error code.
6795;182;%1: Execute SERCOS user command %2 failed (overwritten command error code);Execution of a Sercos-command triggered by applicatioin failed. Command error text could not be read because of a different error with higher priority.;Parameter values must be changed. For further analysis resolve the error with higher priority first.
6795;183;%1: Execute SERCOS user command %2 failed (unknown command error code %3);Execution of a Sercos-command triggered by applicatioin failed, unknown command error code;Parameter values must be changed. The meaning of the error code can be found in the documentation of the device.
